        "title": "Differentiating a Quotient Containing Other Functions"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "0ccc7087-f756-5d26-8bb6-8f7ad6f2e5bb",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\tan x}{x}$,  find ${f}^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\tan x$ and $v(x)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (x)-(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (x)^{\\prime}}{(x)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\sec^{2}x\\cdot x-\\tan x\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{x\\sec^{2}x-\\tan x}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "635b27ed-e6d3-587d-9289-4a69ec41aaad",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "89189f30-bdb4-5f22-9584-be308fa760ab",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{x \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + x - \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}"
              }
            ],
